content.text:
Orders table body rows now have 6px of space above and below the text, down from 12px. The heading row is unchanged, and so is the pricing page, which uses the same table style.

I added this rule at the end of `site/css/pages.css`, scoped to `.page-orders`:

```css
.page-orders .table tbody td {
  padding-top: 6px;
  padding-bottom: 6px;
}
```

The functional tests pass (12 of 12). In the visual tests, 10 of 12 snapshots are unchanged. The two that changed are `orders__desktop` and `orders__phone`, and the only difference is that each page is 72px shorter, which is the expected effect of the tighter rows. I haven't approved the new baselines, because that needs your sign-off. If the compact rows look right to you, say so and I'll approve them, or you can run `npx testivai approve orders__desktop` and `npx testivai approve orders__phone` yourself.

STATUS: DONE

